## [3.0.0] - 2024-01-15

###  Major Release - Event-Driven Architecture

This is a complete rewrite of KingsLibrary with a focus on modern, event-driven architecture using CSS classes for automatic functionality binding.

### Added

- **Event-Driven Design**: All utilities now work through CSS classes with automatic event delegation
- **Framework Agnostic**: Works with Bootstrap, Tailwind, Bulma, or any CSS framework
- **NPM Package**: Proper package structure for distribution via NPM and CDN
- **TypeScript Definitions**: Full TypeScript support with detailed type definitions
- **Modular Architecture**: Clean separation of utilities with `BaseUtility` class
- **Zero Configuration**: Works out of the box with sensible defaults

#### New Utilities
- `FormUtility`: AJAX forms with validation (`.ajax-form`, `.validate-field`)
- `TableUtility`: DataTables integration with export (`.datatable-init`, `.export-excel`)
- `NotificationUtility`: Toast notifications and alerts (`.toast-trigger`, `.alert-trigger`)
- `PasswordUtility`: Password strength and visibility (`.password-strength`, `.password-toggle`)
- `MediaUtility`: File uploads and drag-drop (`.file-upload`, `.file-drop-zone`)
- `ActionUtility`: Generic AJAX actions (`.ajax-action`, `.confirm-action`)
- `ImageUtility`: Image previews and galleries (`.image-preview`, `.image-gallery`)
- `ChatUtility`: Real-time messaging interface (`.chat-container`, `.chat-send`)
- `PageletUtility`: Dynamic content loading (`.pagelet-trigger`, `.pagelet-clear`)

#### Build System
- **Vite Configuration**: Modern build system with multiple output formats
- **UMD Build**: `kingslibrary.umd.js` for AMD/CommonJS/Global usage
- **ES Module Build**: `kingslibrary.esm.js` for modern bundlers
- **IIFE Build**: `kingslibrary.min.js` for direct browser usage
- **Source Maps**: Full source map support for debugging
- **Minification**: Optimized builds with Terser

#### Documentation
- **Comprehensive README**: Framework integration examples and API reference
- **Interactive Playground**: Live demonstration environment
- **CDN Ready**: Available via jsDelivr and unpkg
- **Migration Guide**: Backward compatibility and migration path from v2.x

### 🔄 Changed

- **Breaking**: Function-based API replaced with CSS class-based approach
- **Breaking**: Manual initialization replaced with automatic event delegation
- **Improved**: Better error handling and validation feedback
- **Enhanced**: More intuitive data attribute configuration
- **Modernized**: ES6+ syntax with backward compatibility

### 🔧 Migration from v2.x

#### Before (v2.x)
```javascript
// Manual function calls required
insert_data('../api/user/create', 'user_form');
checknewpass('password1', 'password2', 'error_msg');
ExportToExcel('myTable');
```

#### After (v3.0)
```html
<!-- Automatic functionality through CSS classes -->
<form class="ajax-form" data-url="/api/user/create">
    <input name="name" class="validate-field" required>
    <button type="submit">Create User</button>
</form>

<input type="password" class="password-strength">
<button class="export-excel" data-table="#myTable">Export Excel</button>
```

### 📦 Distribution

- **NPM**: `npm install kingslibrary`
- **CDN (jsDelivr)**: `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/kingslibrary@3/dist/kingslibrary.min.js`
- **CDN (unpkg)**: `https://unpkg.com/kingslibrary@3/dist/kingslibrary.min.js`

### 🏗️ Technical Details

- **Dependencies**: jQuery 3.6+ (external)
- **Browser Support**: Modern browsers (ES6+)
- **Bundle Size**: ~62KB minified, ~17KB gzipped
- **License**: MIT

### 🔧 Configuration

```javascript
KingsLibrary.config({
    apiBaseUrl: '/api',
    notifications: { position: 'top-right' },
    forms: { validateOnBlur: true },
    tables: { pageLength: 25 },
    debug: false
});
```

### 🎯 Backward Compatibility

All v2.x functions are still available for gradual migration:
- `Toastz()` - Legacy notification function
- `ExportToExcel()` - Legacy export function  
- `insert_data()` - Legacy form submission
- `checknewpass()` - Legacy password validation

---

## Previous Versions

### [2.x] - Legacy Version
- Function-based API
- Manual initialization required
- Limited framework integration
- Basic utilities for forms, tables, and notifications

### [1.x] - Initial Release
- Basic JavaScript utilities
- Simple function-based approach
- Limited feature set